---
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/dotfiles-agents-env-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/dotfiles-agents-env-dark.svg?raw';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={400}
  caption="One rendered file feeds two environments, and the check has to read each one."
>
  The repo holds a template of 1Password references. Running op inject renders
  it into a local env file that exists on this Mac only: plaintext, mode 600,
  not in git. Terminal sessions get the values when shell startup reads the
  file. Desktop apps get them when a LaunchAgent sets each value in the GUI
  launch environment. The installer's check reads both: its own process
  environment and the GUI launch environment.
</Diagram>
